{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Repair bin/upgrade.py and upgrade the catalog from v1 to v2 while preserving existing IDs and descriptions, adding a non-null nonnegative price_cents field initialized to zero.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The repaired script was installed and the live upgrade completed. The resulting database has schema version 2, retains products (1, Paper) and (2, Tape), initializes both prices to 0, defaults new prices to 0, rejects negative and NULL values, and passes integrity checks. The same state remained healthy after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-7cca9c45bc7f43e9","cmd-636e27f8add34a17","cmd-de6189d1ba034637"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Make the upgrade transactional so schema_version advances only after the whole upgrade succeeds and a failed attempt leaves the v1 database usable.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The script encloses schema alteration and version update in one explicit transaction with rollback on exceptions. A forced failure during the version update rolled back the preceding ALTER: version stayed 1, the original two-column schema and rows remained, integrity was OK, and a v1 write succeeded.","evidence_ids":["cmd-7cca9c45bc7f43e9","cmd-74959c3621bd473a"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Make the migration safe to repeat.","status":"satisfied","summary":"A second execution completed successfully with exactly three columns, unchanged rows, version 2, and an unchanged database checksum. A further post-restart execution was also successful and checksum-neutral.","evidence_ids":["cmd-7e0ec3ef887f42a7","cmd-de6189d1ba034637"]},{"id":"R4","requirement":"Keep the installed operating-system release and kernel and use software compatible with the legacy platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The executor used the platform's installed Python 3 and SQLite library without package or platform replacement. RHEL 10.0 and kernel 6.12.0-55.9.1.el10_0 were directly observed both before work and after restart, matching the life